*spawn* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

''spawn(args)''

Starts a detached background process. The spawned process runs in a new session
and is not affected by the parent.

*Parameters:*
- ''args'': List of strings with program and arguments (first element is program path)

*Returns:*
- Number: Process ID (PID) of the spawned process
- ''err'' on failure

*Errors:*
- Runtime error if args is not a list
- Runtime error if any element in args is not a string
- Runtime error if args list is empty

*Environment propagation:*

The current process environment is passed to the new program.
